1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:07,567
Repair shops still run critical work across disconnected calendars, inspections, messages, and parts portals.

2
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:11,833
ZOL brings that journey into one intelligent operating system.

3
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:19,816
We will follow a vehicle from appointment through diagnosis, approval, repair, payment, and long-term customer care.

4
00:00:22,463 --> 00:00:25,187
The day begins on ZOL's live dashboard.

5
00:00:25,187 --> 00:00:32,521
Managers immediately see appointments, vehicles in the shop, approvals, revenue, and technician workload.

6
00:00:32,521 --> 00:00:38,178
The repair-order pipeline replaces status meetings with a shared source of truth.

7
00:00:38,178 --> 00:00:45,163
Every number comes from the shop's Cloud SQL database, so the team acts on current operational data.

8
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:53,511
Appointments connect the customer, vehicle, concern, time, and technician before arrival.

9
00:00:53,511 --> 00:00:57,695
At check-in, the advisor records mileage, fuel, damage, and notes.

10
00:00:57,695 --> 00:01:07,520
ZOL creates the repair order automatically, preserving one continuous record without re-entering information or losing the customer's original description.

11
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:21,270
The repair order is ZOL's central workspace, combining status, diagnostics, inspection, estimate, parts, conversation, and billing.

12
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:29,578
For this Chevrolet Sonic, the technician entered check-engine codes, rough-idle symptoms, and fuel-trim observations.

13
00:01:29,578 --> 00:01:36,963
ZOL ranks possible causes and recommends an ordered test plan, always requiring technician verification.

14
00:01:36,963 --> 00:01:41,508
The digital inspection captures green, yellow, and red findings.

15
00:01:41,508 --> 00:01:48,467
Its customer summary uses only findings the technician entered and never invents vehicle problems.

16
00:01:54,759 --> 00:02:01,830
Verified recommendations become an itemized estimate with labor, parts, tax, and transparent demo pricing.

17
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:09,502
The mobile customer portal shows the original concern, inspection, diagnostic context, recommended work, and total.

18
00:02:09,502 --> 00:02:13,638
An approval updates the estimate and repair order immediately.

19
00:02:13,638 --> 00:02:19,309
Declined work becomes a responsible CRM follow-up instead of disappearing into notes.

20
00:02:21,974 --> 00:02:24,295
Approved work moves into execution.

21
00:02:24,295 --> 00:02:29,005
Parts are tracked from needed through ordered, received, and installed.

22
00:02:29,005 --> 00:02:35,903
The mobile-friendly technician board organizes jobs by owner, urgency, approval, and parts availability.

23
00:02:35,903 --> 00:02:44,724
Managers see bottlenecks without interrupting technicians, while technicians move repairs through quality check and ready for pickup.

24
00:02:47,999 --> 00:02:52,945
Completed work converts into an invoice without re-keying line items.

25
00:02:52,945 --> 00:02:58,321
ZOL supports Stripe test payments and a labeled demo provider for this MVP.

26
00:02:58,321 --> 00:03:05,704
Payment marks the invoice paid, closes the repair order, and records the transaction without card data.

27
00:03:05,704 --> 00:03:12,442
The CRM turns declined services, maintenance needs, and post-repair check-ins into follow-ups.

28
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:16,599
AI drafts friendly outreach using only verified shop data.

29
00:03:20,662 --> 00:03:23,956
Finally, owners get a controlled AI shop assistant.

30
00:03:23,956 --> 00:03:29,963
Managers can ask about approvals, tomorrow's arrivals, delayed parts, or technician workload.

31
00:03:29,963 --> 00:03:35,194
Answers use safe, tenant-scoped functions rather than generated database queries.

32
00:03:35,194 --> 00:03:48,112
ZOL connects the customer-to-cash workflow today, with clean paths to production payments, messaging, storage, and supplier data: a foundation for a more efficient shop and a better-informed customer.

